## /extract-content Command (also handles /extract-media)

When the user types `/extract-content` or `/extract-media`, run the unified content extraction pipeline.

### What it does

Scans `raw/` for new files, extracts readable content, creates wiki source pages, and updates index/log.

| File Type | Extensions | Extraction Method |
|-----------|-----------|-------------------|
| Video/Audio | .mp4 .mkv .webm .avi .mov .m4v .mp3 .wav .m4a .ogg .flac | faster-whisper transcription (local) |
| Images | .png .jpg .jpeg .webp .gif | Metadata + description (full analysis via /graphify) |
| PDFs | .pdf | Text extraction (PyMuPDF/pypdf) |
| Office | .docx .xlsx | python-docx / openpyxl → markdown |

### Usage patterns

| User says | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| `/extract-content` | `python scripts/extract_content.py` — all new files |
| `/extract-content --type video` | Only video/audio files |
| `/extract-content --type image` | Only images |
| `/extract-content --type pdf` | Only PDFs |
| `/extract-content --type doc` | Only .docx/.xlsx |
| `/extract-content --model medium` | Better whisper accuracy for technical content |
| `/extract-content --url <youtube-url>` | Download YouTube audio + transcribe + ingest |
| `/extract-content --language en` | Force English (default: auto-detect) |
| `/extract-content --dry-run` | Preview without processing |
| `/extract-media` | Alias: `python scripts/extract_media.py` (video/audio only) |
| `/extract-media --url <youtube-url>` | Alias: download + transcribe YouTube |

### Execution

```powershell
python scripts/extract_content.py [args]
```

### Output locations

- Extracts: `raw/extracts/<slug>.md`
- Wiki pages: `wiki/sources/extract-<slug>.md`
- Manifest: `scripts/.content_manifest.json`

### After extraction

1. Review wiki pages in `wiki/sources/extract-*`
2. Fill in "Key Points" sections
3. Add `[[wikilinks]]` to connect concepts
4. Run `/graphify ./raw --update` to refresh the knowledge graph with new content
5. Run `/graphify-to-wiki` to sync graph insights back into wiki (entities, concepts, synthesis pages)

### Note on images and PDFs

The local extraction captures text and metadata. For **full concept extraction** from images (diagrams, screenshots) and PDFs (citations, relationships), run `/graphify ./raw --update` in Cursor chat — this uses Claude Vision and LLM extraction.
